<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
     gtaxlwifi (§47): this is not a PC.

     device/mainline/generic/device.mk copies `pc_core_hardware.xml`, which
     is the hardware profile of a PC and declares `android.hardware.type.pc`.
     On a tablet the feature is false, and in the profile Play receives at
     check-in it sits alongside the absence of `android.hardware.touchscreen`:
     together they make almost every app show up as unsupported (Aurora
     Store: «app not supported»).

     The touchscreen is declared with the stock AOSP file,
     `android.hardware.touchscreen.multitouch.jazzhand.xml`, copied by the
     `device.mk` next to this one: `getevent -pl` on `stmfts` gives
     ABS_MT_SLOT min 0 max 9, i.e. ten distinct fingers. There is no stock
     file to remove a feature declared elsewhere, and that is the only
     reason this file exists.

     `unavailable-feature` does not depend on the reading order: SystemConfig
     collects the features from all partitions and only at the end applies
     `mUnavailableFeatures` (SystemConfig.java, `removeFeature`). It is
     allowed in /vendor/etc/permissions: `vendorPermissionFlag` contains
     ALLOW_FEATURES.

     The other three are declared by the generic tree or by AOSP although
     the tablet does not have them, measured on 28/09 (funzionalita.md).
     NOT usb.host, even though the port is peripheral-only: SystemServer
     starts UsbService (MTP, USB tethering, USB preferences) only if usb.host
     or usb.accessory is declared. Removed on 29/09, it switched off USB
     management (§68.10).
     - camera.external (generic/device.mk, with `:=`): without host mode no
       USB camera can be connected;
     - virtualization_framework (base_system.mk, APEX com.android.virt):
       S-BOOT enters at EL1, `kvm: HYP mode not available`, /dev/kvm does
       not exist. The only reader in the framework is VirtualMachineManager;
     - location.network (pc_core_hardware.xml): there is no network location
       provider (§54.9).
-->
<permissions>
    <unavailable-feature name="android.hardware.type.pc" />
    <unavailable-feature name="android.hardware.camera.external" />
    <unavailable-feature name="android.software.virtualization_framework" />
    <unavailable-feature name="android.hardware.location.network" />
</permissions>
